--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
awplus(config)#username ckp7 privilege 7 password ckPriv7pass
  % Only the following privilege levels are allowed in crypto secure-mode:
  % Privilege level 1
  % Privilege level 15
  Control, in the same console batch two seconds later:
awplus(config)#username ckp1 privilege 1 password ckPriv1pass
  <-- accepted, and it appears in the running configuration
  => STEP N6 PASS: the DUT refuses privilege 7 by name and accepts privilege 1 in the same
     breath. The same privilege-7 command was accepted with no comment in normal mode
     (STEP 0), and the privilege-7 user that already existed was thrown out at the restart
     with the device's own reason, `-- Privilege level 15` (STEP N3). Three pieces of
     evidence, all pointing the same way.

     NOT RUN: the rule that `enable password` must be at least 8 characters.
     `enable password short1` returned `% Password must be at least 8 characters` in secure
     mode. But this unit already carried `security-password minimum-length 8` before the
     case started, and that setting produces the same refusal in normal mode. So the
     refusal cannot be attributed to secure mode on this unit. Removing
     `security-password minimum-length` would separate the two causes, but it would weaken
     a standing security setting on a shared bench, so it was not done.

