--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  | clause                            | does secure mode do it on this unit?         | how it was proved                                   |
  | --------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
  | Disable Telnet                    | YES for the server. The client is NOT         | a telnet login that worked became `Connection       |
  |                                   | disabled (F-2)                                | refused`, which is a TCP reset                      |
  | Disable SNMPv1 and v2             | YES                                           | an SNMP GET that returned the software version      |
  |                                   |                                               | stopped answering, and the community was deleted    |
  |                                   |                                               | from the configuration                              |
  | All privilege levels except 1     | YES                                           | privilege 7 refused by name, privilege 1 accepted   |
  | and 15                            |                                               | in the same breath, and the existing privilege-7    |
  |                                   |                                               | user deleted at boot                                |
  | Weak crypto (MD5, RSA1, DSA)      | MD5 yes. RSA1 and DSA: not applicable (F-4)   | NTP MD5 and SNMPv3 MD5 both refused by name, with   |
  |                                   |                                               | SHA1 and SHA-256 accepted. RSA1 and DSA cannot be   |
  |                                   |                                               | generated on this build in either mode, so secure   |
  |                                   |                                               | mode withdraws nothing                              |

  One rule the title does not mention is enforced more strictly than the documentation
  says: SHA-1 is refused too (F-3). SNMPv3 on this unit means SHA-256 or nothing.

